{"tool_name":"sdm2","contents":["oeb","bioschemas","biotools"],"fetched_metadata":{"biotools":{"id":"sdm2","home":"https://compbio.medschl.cam.ac.uk/sdm2/","summary":"A server for predicting effects of mutations on protein stability","addition_date":"2023-08-29T21:12:45.977710Z","last_update_date":"2025-01-08T14:32:09.070558Z","version":["2.0"],"collections":["3D-BioInfo"],"biotools_curie":"biotools:sdm2","cost":"Free of charge","credit":[{"email":"app41@cam.ac.uk","name":"ARUN PRASAD PANDURANGAN","note":"Computational Biologist at the University of Cambridge","orcidid":"https://orcid.org/0000-0001-7168-7143","typeEntity":"Person","typeRole":["Developer","Maintainer","Primary contact"],"url":"https://www.infectiousdisease.cam.ac.uk/directory/apandura%40mrc-lmb.cam.ac.uk"}],"documentation":[{"type":["Quick start guide"],"url":"https://compbio.medschl.cam.ac.uk/sdm2/help"}],"edit_permission":{"type":"private"},"function":[{"operation":[{"term":"Variant effect prediction","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_0331"}]}],"name":"SDM","operating_system":["Linux"],"owner":"apandura","publication":[{"doi":"10.1093/nar/gkx439","metadata":{"abstract":"Here, we report a webserver for the improved SDM, used for predicting the effects of mutations on protein stability. As a pioneering knowledge-based approach, SDM has been highlighted as the most appropriate method to use in combination with many other approaches. We have updated the environment-specific amino-acid substitution tables based on the current expanded PDB (a 5-fold increase in information), and introduced new residue-conformation and interaction parameters, including packing density and residue depth. The updated server has been extensively tested using a benchmark containing 2690 point mutations from 132 different protein structures. The revised method correlates well against the hypothetical reverse mutations, better than comparable methods built using machine-learning approaches, highlighting the strength of our knowledge-based approach for identifying stabilising mutations. Given a PDB file (a Protein Data Bank file format containing the 3D coordinates of the protein atoms), and a point mutation, the server calculates the stability difference score between the wildtype and mutant protein.","authors":[{"name":"Ascher D.B."},{"name":"Blundell T.L."},{"name":"Ochoa-Montano B."},{"name":"Pandurangan A.P."}],"citationCount":374,"date":"2017-07-03T00:00:00Z","journal":"Nucleic Acids Research","title":"SDM: A server for predicting effects of mutations on protein stability"},"note":"SDM: a server for predicting effects of mutations on protein stability","pmcid":"PMC5793720","pmid":"28525590","type":["Method"],"version":"2.0"}]},"bioschemas":{"name":"SDM","home":"https://bio.tools/sdm2","version":"2.0","summary":"A server for predicting effects of mutations on protein stability","tool_type":"sc:SoftwareApplication"},"oeb":{"metrics":[{"@id":"https://openebench.bsc.es/monitor/metrics/biotools:sdm2:2.0/undefined/compbio.medschl.cam.ac.uk","@license":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/","@nmsp":"biotools","@type":"metrics","deprecated":true,"project":{"build":{},"deployment":{},"publications":[{"entries":[{"cit_count":254,"citations":[{"count":1,"year":"-1"},{"count":9,"year":"2026"},{"count":14,"year":"2018"},{"count":19,"year":"2025"},{"count":26,"year":"2019"},{"count":26,"year":"2024"},{"count":34,"year":"2023"},{"count":37,"year":"2022"},{"count":40,"year":"2020"},{"count":48,"year":"2021"}],"doi":"10.1093/nar/gkx439","pmcid":"PMC5793720","pmid":"28525590","ref_count":58,"refs":[{"count":1,"year":"-1"},{"count":1,"year":"1990"},{"count":1,"year":"1992"},{"count":1,"year":"1996"},{"count":1,"year":"1997"},{"count":1,"year":"1999"},{"count":1,"year":"2003"},{"count":1,"year":"2005"},{"count":1,"year":"2007"},{"count":1,"year":"2008"},{"count":2,"year":"1993"},{"count":2,"year":"2004"},{"count":2,"year":"2013"},{"count":2,"year":"2014"},{"count":3,"year":"1998"},{"count